Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns & their potential usage for the requested task  
(only listing those actually needed to carry‑out the steps that were described):

• WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_VECTORS_US.NATURE  
  – "id": unique article id (filter on the target id and return in final list)  
  – "date": publication date (to be shown in result)  
  – "title": article title (to be shown in result)  
  – "body": full text that will be tokenised (main text to process)  

• WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_FREQUENCIES  
  – "word": word string (join key)  
  – "frequency": overall corpus frequency (used for weighting ‑ divide vector by frequency^0.4)  

• WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_VECTORS_US.GLOVE_VECTORS  
  – "word": word string (join key)  
  – "vector": 300‑dimensional embedding (to be weighted / summed / normalised)  

Typical filter/conditions likely to be used  
• WHERE "id" = '8a78ef2d-d5f7-4d2d-9b47-5adb25cbd373'  (target article)  
• JOINs on the word field between token list, WORD_FREQUENCIES, and GLOVE_VECTORS  
• Tokenisation via `spider2-public-data.word_vectors_us.tokenise_no_stop()` UDF  
• LIMIT 10 / ORDER BY similarity DESC when returning final list  

